Nmap scans the top 1000 ports by default. Convenient but makes it easier to miss extra information.
      nmap -p- --min-rate 1000 10.113.146.201
            # Full port scan (aggressive speed)
            # --min-rate 1000: Forces Nmap to send ≥1000 packets/sec 
            #                  (bypasses default throttling on slow networks)
            
Provided command can be used after an initial port scan, and manual enumeration, to see if anything was missed. 

Learned through missed information on mustacchio, specifically not knowing where an admin credential can be used. 
